# ShiftPatch environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for a new setup, or edit your existing file.
# Fill in both required values before pnpm dev. For deploys, set them on the host.
# Restart after edits. Shell exports override .env.local.
# Keep DB URLs and keys server-side (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix) and out of Git.

# App: required for sign-in and database-backed features

# Use a fresh Postgres DB. The role needs to create tables, indexes, and sequences.
# On first use, the app creates the schema and seeds demo accounts and shifts.
# Older incompatible schemas need a migration.
# Local example: postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5432/shiftpatch_dev
# For Neon, copy the full URI from Connect, including query parameters.
# Use a dev database separate from any deployment.
DATABASE_URL=

# Signs and verifies API JWTs. Browser sign-in needs it too.
# No default, 32+ characters. Generate with openssl rand -hex 32.
# Changing the key invalidates old JWTs.
JWT_SECRET=

# App: optional

# Client address header for login rate limits (default x-real-ip).
# Only use a header your trusted proxy overwrites. Without it, attempts
# for each email share the same unknown address.
# TRUSTED_IP_HEADER=x-real-ip

# Playwright: supply these in the shell when running pnpm test:e2e directly.
# Playwright skips .env.local and resets the DB before each test.
# Use a disposable DB separate from dev and deployed apps.
# make db-up && make e2e supplies the URL below and generates a key unless
# you set a nonempty E2E_JWT_SECRET.
# export E2E_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres@localhost:5433/shiftpatch_e2e
# export E2E_JWT_SECRET="$(openssl rand -hex 32)"

# CI and Postgres container settings (set by Make or GitHub Actions)
# GitHub Actions sets CI. Any value, even blank, enables one retry and CI
# reports, forbids focused tests, and disables server reuse.
# CI=1
# GitHub Actions provides GITHUB_ENV to pass the generated key to later steps.
# Make and CI pass these settings to Docker. .env.local has no effect here.
# POSTGRES_DB names the test DB. Use trust for passwordless access only in a
# disposable test container.
# POSTGRES_DB=shiftpatch_e2e
# POSTGRES_HOST_AUTH_METHOD=trust

# Next.js settings
# Export PORT or use pnpm dev --port 3001 (default 3000). PORT in .env.local
# has no effect. Playwright uses 3100.
# PORT=3001
# Let Next.js and the test runner set NODE_ENV and NEXT_RUNTIME.
# Export NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1 to opt out of Next.js telemetry.
# No NEXT_PUBLIC_* settings. The token lifetime and login
# rate limits are set in code.
